cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  isaac-bioresearch: embodied, biologically derived nervous systems
  in NVIDIA Isaac Sim
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Please also cite the underlying connectome and annotation datasets
  directly — see DATA_LICENSES.md. The scientific data is other
  people's work and this repository does not replace it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bacsi
    given-names: Gabor
repository-code: https://github.com/BacheyG/isaac-bioresearch-playground
abstract: >-
  A research and engineering project asking what happens when the
  controller of a simulated animal is derived from the reconstructed
  nervous system of a real one, rather than designed. Provides a
  normalized schema and verified importers for published
  Caenorhabditis elegans connectomes, keeping directly measured
  anatomy strictly separate from published annotations and from
  modelling assumptions, with per-field provenance throughout.
  Long-term goal is a closed sensorimotor loop inside NVIDIA Isaac
  Sim, first for C. elegans and later for Drosophila melanogaster.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - computational neuroscience
  - Caenorhabditis elegans
  - Drosophila melanogaster
  - embodied simulation
  - robotics simulation
  - NVIDIA Isaac Sim
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
